**Finding (preliminary):** Estimate built on a sourced base and an assumed share: about 1,200 papers on galaxy cluster physics among the 18,660 primary astro-ph papers of 2025 (strict range about 950-1,550, i.e. about 5-8%), and about 2,000-3,000 under a broad definition. The survey's central figure of about 1,500 sits at the top of the strict range, so it is somewhat high but not ruled out.
