**Critic, wave 1** — continue: 0 findings stand up to the evidence, 3 questioned ('Astrophysics Wrapped 2025 (arXiv:2602.12303, Sec. 2.1) states that 18,660 papers were uplo': The cited excerpt from tc-261015_2-w1-d-01-15 shows only the title page (chars 0-15000, truncated after the affiliations). It contains neither the 18,660 figure nor the quote on excluding replacements and cross-submissions. The value may well be correct, since it matches the Table 1 sum exactly, but the posted evidence does not show it and no cite() call validated it.; 'Table 1 of arXiv:2602.12303 gives the 2025 primary-subject counts: astro-ph.GA 4,761; astr': The cited excerpt from tc-261015_2-w1-d-01-17 (chars 35000-55000) shows the telescopes and objects section and the Fig. 2 caption, not Table 1. The per-category counts do not appear in it. The numbers are internally consistent: they sum to 18,660, GA+CO = 7,550 (40.5%), and GA+CO+HE = 11,419 (61.2%). That consistency is not evidence of the source values.; 'Estimate built on a sourced base and an assumed share: about 1,200 papers on galaxy cluste': The arithmetic reproduces from the stated assumptions: CO 15-25% gives 418-697, GA 8-12% gives 381-571, HE 3-5% gives 116-193, and others add 30-80, for a total of about 945-1,541. However, the base inputs rest on f-001 and f-002, whose excerpts do not show them. The per-category cluster fractions are unsourced, so the evidence supports none of the cluster-specific content. The broad range of 2,000-3,000 is asserted without any derivation.).

Issues: Quoted values (18,660 and the cross-submission exclusion) are not present in the evidence excerpts. The relevant chunk of 2602.12303 needs to be re-read and passed to cite() so the quote is validated in references.bib.; The Table 1 counts are not in the cited excerpt. The tool call or chunk range containing Table 1 needs to be identified and cited.; The cluster fractions per category (CO 15-25%, GA 8-12%, HE 3-5%) are labelled assumptions with no anchor. The broad range of 2,000-3,000 has no derivation. It also mixes a primary-only base with cross-listed gr-qc and hep-ph papers without quantifying the cross-list contribution. The final number therefore still rests on the survey's unverified 5-8% share..
